      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "1.2 grams. That's all it takes to die from cocaine. In 2024, an estimated 22,174 American lives were lost to cocaine-involved overdoses. Drugs interdicted are lives saved. As America’s maritime counter-drug leader, the U.S. Coast Guard is on the frontlines, interdicting drugs and disrupting criminal networks. Since January 20, we’ve interdicted over 183,000 lbs. of cocaine – enough to kill more than 69 million people.\n\nAcross our borders and maritime approaches, the Coast Guard is seizing cocaine before it reaches our streets, disrupting criminal networks that profit from causing harm, and saving American lives. @DHSgov \n\n#USCG #stopdrugtrafficking #DrugInterdiction",
      "text_resolved": "1.2 grams. That's all it takes to die from cocaine. In 2024, an estimated 22,174 American lives were lost to cocaine-involved overdoses. Drugs interdicted are lives saved. As America’s maritime counter-drug leader, the U.S. Coast Guard is on the frontlines, interdicting drugs and disrupting criminal networks. Since January 20, we’ve interdicted over 183,000 lbs. of cocaine – enough to kill more than 69 million people.\n\nAcross our borders and maritime approaches, the Coast Guard is seizing cocaine before it reaches our streets, disrupting criminal networks that profit from causing harm, and saving American lives. @DHSgov \n\n#USCG #stopdrugtrafficking #DrugInterdiction",
