      "reply_to_account": null,
      "reply_to_account_id": null,
      "quoted_tweet_id": null,
      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "Crisis leadership means being ready for any contingency. As the Nation’s first responder, the Coast Guard saves over 5,000 lives each year and is always ready to lead through crisis.\nNow that hurricane season is here, your preparedness is just as important. Are you ready? Follow these 5 steps to prepare:  1. Develop an Evacuation Plan: Know your zone & practice your route! 2. Assemble Disaster Supplies: Food, water, meds, first-aid kit, flashlights, and batteries. 3. Check Insurance and Possessions: Review your policies and document your belongings. 4. Make an Emergency Contact List: Create and share a list with loved ones. 5. Secure Your Home and Belongings: Trim trees, bring in loose items, and board up windows.  Stay safe and informed this hurricane season. Follow us for updates! #HurricanePrep #USCG #AmericasFirstResponder  #ValuetoNation",
      "text_resolved": "Crisis leadership means being ready for any contingency. As the Nation’s first responder, the Coast Guard saves over 5,000 lives each year and is always ready to lead through crisis.\nNow that hurricane season is here, your preparedness is just as important. Are you ready? Follow these 5 steps to prepare:  1. Develop an Evacuation Plan: Know your zone & practice your route! 2. Assemble Disaster Supplies: Food, water, meds, first-aid kit, flashlights, and batteries. 3. Check Insurance and Possessions: Review your policies and document your belongings. 4. Make an Emergency Contact List: Create and share a list with loved ones. 5. Secure Your Home and Belongings: Trim trees, bring in loose items, and board up windows.  Stay safe and informed this hurricane season. Follow us for updates! #HurricanePrep #USCG #AmericasFirstResponder  #ValuetoNation",
